  "memorial_type": "Board / Plaque / Tablet",
  "memorial_details": "Wall mounted, landscape orientated incised stone tablets, enclosed by a moulded stone frame. Inscription infilled with black paint.",
  "inscription": "WORLD WAR 1939-1945. / REMEMBER / SERGEANT CHARLES HENRY HILTON, / ROYAL AIR FORCE, OF YELDEN. / KILLED ON ACTIVE SERVICE / 24TH AUGUST 1943 / EDWIN KEITH, AGED 14 YEARS. / MONICA RUTH PHILLIPS, AGED 4 YEARS / OF YELDEN. / KILLED BY AN AIRCRAFT WHICH CRASHED / NEAR THIS CHURCH 24TH MARCH 1944. In memory of the men who died on the night of 24th March 1944 when Boeing B-17G Flying Fortress serial number 42-97578 of 422nd Squadron 305th Bomb Group crashed just north of Yelden Church. Aircrew: SGT W D SELLERS / SGT J E GEORGE / SGT J N A GRUGNALE / SGT L J JUDD / SGT C W LEAKE / SGT J H LEHR / SGT K I MACE / SGT D C PARRISH / SGT D M REMENTERIA / SGT D E RISHEL / SGT M SILBER 1121st Quartermaster Company (names)",
